  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "EVA recording console",
    "overview": "A narrow native utility carries EVA's warm cream identity above an ink workspace. Cobalt gives actions and selection a clear visual weight; compact media and source rows keep recording work legible without decorative card stacks.\n\nThe brand is concentrated in the heart and condensed EVA CLIPPER wordmark. Russian controls use Segoe UI, explicit labels and familiar Windows keyboard behavior. Flat rectangular actions coexist with round slider thumbs and pill switches because those shapes communicate different operations.\n\nThis is the implemented 3.1 system extracted from `src/Panel.cs`, `src/Controls.cs` and `src/Overlay.cs`, with the embedded font confirmed in `scripts/build.ps1`. The palette and display family match the public [EVA site](https://theeva.ai), read on 2026-10-09. Sampled native captures are `.impeccable/review-v31/home.png`, `video-720.png` and `video-bottom-720.png`; the available review set also contains all five settings tabs at 440 × 1000. The harness renders production controls with synthetic engine and device state. It demonstrates interface appearance, not capture compatibility, successful recording or exact synchronization.\n\nThe 3.1.1 repaint and motion behavior is implemented in `src/Controls.cs`, `src/Panel.cs` and `src/PanelMotion.cs`. The current production-control fixture matrix is `.impeccable/review-v311/{home.png,Источники.png,Видео.png,Аудио.png,Файлы.png,Клавиши.png,video-720.png,video-bottom-720.png}`, at 440px wide and 1000px or 720px high with synthetic engine and device state. `tests/PanelChecks.cs` covers translated and clipped toggle paint, removal of old labels, continuous reversals, duplicate targets and irregular frame timing. Fixture appearance and callback timings do not establish product FPS or direct live hover behavior; Computer Use hover capture remains pending.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cream masthead, ink canvas, warm text and cobalt actions.",
      "A fixed-width right-edge panel with persistent settings navigation and Apply footer.",
      "Embedded Bebas Neue branding with a Segoe UI interface.",
      "Owner-drawn selectors, slim sliders and switches with visible keyboard focus.",
      "A reversible reveal at a fixed window position and settings that scroll without wheel edits."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Brand and State Rule",
        "body": "Cream and the heart identify EVA; cobalt marks primary actions, selection and enabled settings. Recording red identifies the stop action after engine confirmation; warning text identifies current errors or unavailable sources.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Faces Rule",
        "body": "Use Bebas Neue for the EVA CLIPPER wordmark only. Use Segoe UI for Russian headings, controls, values and help text.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fixed Chrome Rule",
        "body": "Keep the masthead, five settings tabs and Apply action outside the scrolling body. Short work areas change the visible content height, not the panel width or navigation order.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Surface Rule",
        "body": "Separate controls through fill, spacing and typography. The native system has no authored shadow, glass blur or decorative card stack.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Wheel Safety Rule",
        "body": "The wheel scrolls the settings body without changing a value, even over a selector popup or slider. Changing a parameter requires an explicit click, drag or keyboard action.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the cream masthead, EVA heart, ink canvas and cobalt action hierarchy.",
      "Do keep the wordmark in the embedded Bebas Neue face and Russian controls in Segoe UI.",
      "Do retain the 440px panel and fixed settings tabs, Apply action and status area.",
      "Do make parameter edits explicit and preserve visible keyboard focus.",
      "Do show recording, replay, source availability and disabled actions from confirmed engine state.",
      "Do use real local media in the gallery and keep private captures out of public design assets."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't replace the EVA heart with a text glyph or redraw action icons as font characters.",
      "Don't apply rectangular control geometry to switch tracks or slider thumbs.",
      "Don't add ornamental shadows, glass layers or card stacks to this utility.",
      "Don't turn a wheel gesture into a selector or slider edit.",
      "Don't imply a successful save while replay is off or before the engine confirms completion.",
      "Don't treat a UI screenshot as proof of borderless capture compatibility or frame-accurate synchronization."
    ]
  }
